            {
              "$type": "Models.Core.Simulation, Models",
              "Name": "_Dwarf",
              "ResourceName": null,
              "Children": [
                {
                  "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
                  "Text": "*\tBased on Green et al 2013 - PFR report for the Hawkes Bay Regional Council\n\n* \tLocation: Hastings, NZ \n\n*\tCultivar: Pink Lady\n\n*\tTranspiration measured using sap flow sensors.\n\n\n++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n\nThe apple experiments were carried out at Mr Apple’s Close Orchard near Whakatu, on a free draining Hastings silt loam. Two sites were chosen: one block was planted in 12-year-old ‘Royal Gala’ and the other block was planted in 8-year-old Pink Lady® on a dwarfing root stock. Irrigation was via micro-sprinklers and the strategy was to apply water at a rate of 10–25 mm as required. The irrigation scheduling was provided by AgFirst consultants who also monitored soil water contents at some, but not all, the orchard blocks",
                  "Name": "ExperimentDescription",
                  "ResourceName": null,
                  "Children": [],
                  "Enabled": true,
                  "ReadOnly": false
                },
                {
